1747 ( [LINK: (MDCCXLVII) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_numerals] ) was a  [LINK: (common year starting on Sunday) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Common_year_starting_on_Sunday]  of the  [LINK: (Gregorian calendar) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gregorian_calendar]  and a  [LINK: (common year starting on Thursday) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Common_year_starting_on_Thursday]  of the  [LINK: (Julian calendar) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Julian_calendar] , the 1747th year of the  [LINK: (Common Era) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Common_Era]  (CE) and  [LINK: (Anno Domini) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anno_Domini]  (AD) designations, the 747th  year of the  [LINK: (2nd millennium) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2nd_millennium] , the 47th  year of the  [LINK: (18th century) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/18th_century] , and the  8th   year of the  [LINK: (1740s) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1740s]  decade. As of the start of 1747, the Gregorian calendar was 11 days ahead of the Julian calendar, which remained in localized use until 1923.


# EVENTS #

[LINK: (January 31) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_31]  –  The first  [LINK: (venereal diseases) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Venereal_disease]  clinic opens at  [LINK: (London Lock Hospital) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/London_Lock_Hospital] .

[LINK: (February 11) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_11]  –  [LINK: (King George's War) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/King_George%27s_War] : A combined French and Indian force, commanded by Captain  [LINK: (Nicolas Antoine II Coulon de Villiers) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nicolas_Antoine_II_Coulon_de_Villiers] ,  [LINK: (attacks and defeats British troops) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Grand_Pr%C3%A9]  at  [LINK: (Grand-Pré, Nova Scotia) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grand-Pr%C3%A9,_Nova_Scotia] .

[LINK: (March 7) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/March_7]  –  [LINK: (Juan de Arechederra) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Juan_de_Arechederra]  the Spanish  [LINK: (Governor-General of the Philippines) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Governor-General_of_the_Philippines] , combines  his forces with those of Sultan  [LINK: (Azim ud-Din I of Sulu) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Azim_ud-Din_I_of_Sulu]  to suppress the rebellion of the  [LINK: (Moros) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moro_people]  in the  [LINK: (Visayas) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Visayas] . [LINK: ([1]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1747#cite_note-1]

[LINK: (March 19) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/March_19]  –  [LINK: (Simon Fraser) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Simon_Fraser,_11th_Lord_Lovat] , the 79-year old Scottish Lord Lovat, is convicted of high treason for being one of the leaders of the  [LINK: (Jacobite rising of 1745) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jacobite_rising_of_1745]  against King  [LINK: (George II of Great Britain) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/George_II_of_Great_Britain]  and attempting to place the pretender  [LINK: (Charles Edward Stuart) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles_Edward_Stuart]  on the throne. [LINK: ([2]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1747#cite_note-2]   After a seven day trial of impeachment in the  [LINK: (House of Lords) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/House_of_Lords]  and the verdict of guilt, Fraser is sentenced on the same day to be  [LINK: (hanged, drawn and quartered) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hanged,_drawn_and_quartered] ; King George alters Fraser's punishment to  [LINK: (beheading) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Decapitation] , which is carried out publicly on April 9.

[LINK: (April 9) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/April_9]  – The Scottish  [LINK: (Jacobite) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jacobitism]   [LINK: (Lord Lovat) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Simon_Fraser,_11th_Lord_Lovat]  is beheaded at  [LINK: (Tower Hill) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tower_Hill] ,  [LINK: (London) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/London] , for  [LINK: (high treason) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/High_treason] . He was the last person in  [LINK: (Britain) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_Britain]  to be beheaded, although beheading would not be formally abolished until more than 200 years later.

[LINK: (May 14) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/May_14]  –  [LINK: (War of the Austrian Succession) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/War_of_the_Austrian_Succession]  –  [LINK: (First battle of Cape Finisterre) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/First_battle_of_Cape_Finisterre_(1747)] : The British Navy defeats a French fleet.

[LINK: (June 9) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/June_9]  –  [LINK: (Emperor Momozono) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emperor_Momozono_of_Japan]  ascends to the throne of  [LINK: (Japan) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japan] , succeeding  [LINK: (Emperor Sakuramachi) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emperor_Sakuramachi_of_Japan] .

[LINK: (June 24) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/June_24] – [LINK: (October 14) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/October_14]  – The  [LINK: (English) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/England]  ships Dobbs galley and California, under Captains William Moore and Francis Smith, explore  [LINK: (Hudson Bay) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hudson_Bay] , discovering there is no  [LINK: (Northwest Passage) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Northwest_Passage]  by this route.

[LINK: (July 2) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/July_2]  –  [LINK: (War of the Austrian Succession) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/War_of_the_Austrian_Succession]  –  [LINK: (Battle of Lauffeld) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Lauffeld] : France defeats the combined armies of  [LINK: (Hanover) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hanover] ,  [LINK: (Great Britain) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_Britain]  and the  [LINK: (Netherlands) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Netherlands] .

[LINK: (August 15) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/August_15]  –  [LINK: (Great Britain) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_Britain] ,  [LINK: (Russia) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russian_Empire]  and the  [LINK: (Dutch Republic) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dutch_Republic]  sign the  [LINK: (Convention of Saint Petersburg (1747)) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Convention_of_Saint_Petersburg_(1747)] .

[LINK: (August 24) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/August_24]  –  [LINK: (Seyyid Abdullah Pasha) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seyyid_Abdullah_Pasha] , the Turkish Governor of Cyprus, becomes the new  [LINK: (Grand Vizier of the Ottoman Empire) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grand_Vizier_of_the_Ottoman_Empire]  and serves until 1750.

[LINK: (September 13) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/September_13]  – The  [LINK: (Netherlands) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Netherlands]  city of  [LINK: (Bergen op Zoom) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bergen_op_Zoom]  falls to the Army of France after a 70 day  [LINK: (siege) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Siege_of_Bergen_op_Zoom_(1747)]  during the  [LINK: (War of the Austrian Succession) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/War_of_the_Austrian_Succession] . [LINK: ([3]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1747#cite_note-3]

[LINK: (September 21) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/September_21]  – A hurricane in the Caribbean Sea sinks 11 British ships[ [LINK: (dubious) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Accuracy_dispute#Disputed_statement]  –  [LINK: (discuss) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:1747#Dubious] ], most of them off the coast of  [LINK: (Saint Kitts) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saint_Kitts] .

[LINK: (October 1) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/October_1]  – On the 7th day of Shawwal, 1160 A.H., Pashtun chieftains in  [LINK: (Kandahar) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kandahar] , meeting in a special council (a  [LINK: (loya jirga) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Loya_jirga] ) vote to make  [LINK: (Ahmad Shah Durrani) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ahmad_Shah_Durrani]  their leader in  [LINK: (Afghanistan) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Afghanistan]  and beginning the  [LINK: (Durrani Empire) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Durrani_Empire] .

[LINK: (October 21) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/October_21]  – King George II transfers  [LINK: (Thomas Herring) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomas_Herring] , Archbishop of York, to become the new  [LINK: (Archbishop of Canterbury) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Archbishop_of_Canterbury] , three days after the death of  [LINK: (John Potter) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Potter_(bishop)]

[LINK: (October 24) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/October_24]  – A Caribbean Sea hurricane sweeps across  [LINK: (Saint Kitts) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saint_Kitts] , sinking 12 British freighters and one from France. [LINK: ([4]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1747#cite_note-4]

[LINK: (October 25) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/October_25]  –  [LINK: (War of the Austrian Succession) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/War_of_the_Austrian_Succession]  –  [LINK: (Second battle of Cape Finisterre) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Second_battle_of_Cape_Finisterre_(1747)] : The British Navy again defeats a French fleet.

[LINK: (November 9) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/November_9]  –  [LINK: (Rioters) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Riot]  in  [LINK: (Amsterdam) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amsterdam]  demand governmental reform. [LINK: ([5]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1747#cite_note-5]

[LINK: (November 17) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/November_17] – [LINK: (19) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/November_19]  – The  [LINK: (Knowles Riot) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Knowles_Riot]  breaks out in  [LINK: (Boston) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boston] , Massachusetts, protesting  [LINK: (impressment) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Impressment]  into the British  [LINK: (Royal Navy) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Royal_Navy] .

[LINK: (November 22) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/November_22]  – End of  [LINK: (Second Stadtholderless period) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Second_Stadtholderless_period] : Prince  [LINK: (William IV) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_IV,_Prince_of_Orange]  of Orange becomes stadtholder of all the  [LINK: (United Provinces) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dutch_Republic] .

[LINK: (December 7) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/December_7]  –  [LINK: (Benjamin Franklin) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Benjamin_Franklin]  forms the  [LINK: (Pennsylvania) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Province_of_Pennsylvania]   [LINK: (Associators) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Associators] , the first militia in the colony of Pennsylvania, which had no standing militia because of its foundation by pacifistic  [LINK: (Quakers) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quakers] . [LINK: ([6]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1747#cite_note-6]

[LINK: (December 13) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/December_13]  – The ordeal of the  [LINK: (Maryland) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Province_of_Maryland]  freighter  [LINK: (sloop) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sloop]  Endeavour begins when the ship departs  [LINK: (Annapolis) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Annapolis]  for the  [LINK: (West Indies) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/West_Indies]  and encounters a hurricane.  With its masts and rigging torn away, the ship drifts for six months before finally ending up at the island of  [LINK: (Tiree) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tiree]  off the coast of  [LINK: (Scotland) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scotland]  [LINK: ([7]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1747#cite_note-7]

[LINK: (December 27) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/December_27]  – The Parliament of Great Britain amends its  [LINK: (Naturalisation Act 1740) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plantation_Act_1740]  to extend recognition to all non-Anglican Protestant denominations in its colonies. [LINK: ([8]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1747#cite_note-8]

[LINK: (James Lind) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/James_Lind] 's experiment begins to prove that  [LINK: (citrus) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Citrus]  fruits prevent  [LINK: (scurvy) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scurvy] .

[LINK: (War of the Austrian Succession) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/War_of_the_Austrian_Succession] : Spanish troops invade and occupy the coastal towns of  [LINK: (Beaufort) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beaufort,_North_Carolina]  and  [LINK: (Brunswick) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brunswick,_North_Carolina]  in the  [LINK: (Royal Colony of North Carolina) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Royal_Colony_of_North_Carolina] , during what becomes known as the  [LINK: (Spanish Alarm) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spanish_Alarm] . They are later driven out by the local militia.

[LINK: (Samuel Johnson) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Samuel_Johnson]  begins work on  [LINK: (A Dictionary of the English Language) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/A_Dictionary_of_the_English_Language]  in London.


